{"posts":[{"id":"flaglimits_p34_826","t":"Thanks V.\n\nI think i got it now:)","a":"—","d":"","n":"#826","p":34,"im":["885fa214499dd3e132ce9124bbbbb2e9d19f335e"],"m":826},{"id":"flaglimits_p34_827","t":"lv5758\n\nHey DrummerBoy, Im glad that i can help you\n\nIn my opinion i would draw the FL area a lil bit higher as shown in the picture. Hope this is helpful","a":"—","d":"","n":"#827","p":34,"im":["caf86af881f0c0446cee7cb30da1722df222478d"],"m":827},{"id":"flaglimits_p34_828","t":"Thanks V. I thought that the FL is always after the decision to break SR. What should be the rule where we draw the FL?","a":"—","d":"","n":"#828","p":34,"im":[],"m":828},{"id":"flaglimits_p34_829","t":"lv5758\n\nHey DrummerBoy,\n\nIn my opinion its not always after the decision to break SR you see in the FL article its stated \"it makes a decision before it continues down\", so i will try to focus on the decision zone which is as your chart is the DBD (or RBR).","a":"—","d":"","n":"#829","p":34,"im":[],"m":829},{"id":"flaglimits_p34_830","t":"Thanks for your patience, V. Let me try again. I hope I will eventually get the hang of this.","a":"—","d":"","n":"#830","p":34,"im":["949251eb5db89ef4d4cb3a8a1d4414691f6194a1","cb5db29d39244f01c671078cc958f6dc3653f340","d5709a08a5a777b65df1a8e9883580050d5f93a6"],"m":830},{"id":"flaglimits_p34_831","t":"Handing in another homework. Appreciate any feedbacks:)","a":"—","d":"","n":"#831","p":34,"im":["6be5212f61ccea5e11552d2fe4c3453d99e0016a"],"m":831},{"id":"flaglimits_p34_832","t":"rcmacf\n\nDrummer, could you note timeframe and pair on your charts, please, so one can go and investigate them further, if desired? Thanks.\n\nFor the Flag Limit, take a look at how I see it, right or wrong:\n\nreadthemarket.com/index.php/forum/journa...ions?start=175#43419","a":"—","d":"","n":"#832","p":34,"im":[],"m":832},{"id":"flaglimits_p34_833","t":"Thanks for your reply and the link, rcmacf. I will include the TF in my future postings:) I will review the link and hope to do better in my next assignment.:)","a":"—","d":"","n":"#833","p":34,"im":[],"m":833},{"id":"flaglimits_p34_834","t":"Here we go again. Please let me know how i'm doing. Thanks","a":"—","d":"","n":"#834","p":34,"im":["03b7d184d42f995dca21ef1b6ff7978d51d30e5f"],"m":834},{"id":"flaglimits_p34_835","t":"","a":"—","d":"","n":"#835","p":34,"im":["74a95a10e2796cb1fe3b247b47838de04c94a883"],"m":835},{"id":"flaglimits_p34_836","t":"Another example where price consumes the Flag Area. My question is how can i have more certainty that price will react on FTB? Or...am i drawing flag limit wrong?","a":"—","d":"","n":"#836","p":34,"im":["38f463f19ae08dc9c98f6b114686c6f8eada403a"],"m":836},{"id":"flaglimits_p34_837","t":"Muffles\n\nHi DrummerBoy,\n\nThought I might just annotate your charts as to where I believe the FL's which you are trying to analyse are.\n\nCheers, Muffles","a":"—","d":"","n":"#837","p":34,"im":["57036230b283ebb3b9e8540f0192e34c3ee4ce2c","25e9cdcc1043db68255213f7198756cf15a75ba7"],"m":837},{"id":"flaglimits_p34_838","t":"Thanks Muffles. The way you had drawn it, makes more sense:)","a":"—","d":"","n":"#838","p":34,"im":[],"m":838},{"id":"flaglimits_p34_839","t":"sm0uvy\n\nHi, First Attempt at Flag Limit. Any guidance would be appreciated.","a":"—","d":"","n":"#839","p":34,"im":["c6f0b9bdc87a21555d192cc897adad67c9395544"],"m":839},{"id":"flaglimits_p34_840","t":"Pipc\n\nHey sm0uvy, I think the FL is correct, but the FTB occured earlier... the red candle after the FL formed. Just my thoughts.","a":"—","d":"","n":"#840","p":34,"im":[],"m":840},{"id":"flaglimits_p34_841","t":"I agree with you, Pipc","a":"—","d":"","n":"#841","p":34,"im":[],"m":841},{"id":"flaglimits_p34_842","t":"Hi there,\n\njust did some Homework on FL: Flag Limit is at the left edge and inside of blue box, Hope this looks passably alright. Comments are as always very much welcomed!\n\nCopper H1\n\nEURGBP H4\n\nCADJPY H4\n\nAUDUSD Daily\n\nAUDCAD 30min\n\nI have a question about the last chart: To trade the FL, one sets a sell limit at the lower edge of the box and waits for the FTB, right? How do you define your target in that case?\n\nThanks!","a":"—","d":"","n":"#842","p":34,"im":["1633852bdb6fe6ca21d7c4db9bdbdb9d81d8d9cc","f07f80aa77c6fbcd32f734bb3f63d203c86a7139","8b34c552e7d9dcc8e1b3013f3ed81b747cbe8595","044a26cfb50986afedc5412f5f32172a827f52b6","4cb8762597343f6f03c1a689f08205fb60812231"],"m":842},{"id":"flaglimits_p34_843","t":"Hi thetrendsfriend,\n\nWe must go in the lowest timeframe possible to find our FL\n\nEURGBP: 4 hour","a":"—","d":"","n":"#843","p":34,"im":["09e701175e2e422c1c900b461e68f15e7089444a","cf69239bf5797cbdb59a6e94756d061d9299d593","57712e65bb13a3043e337ac37057b20f37cbeba3"],"m":843},{"id":"flaglimits_p34_844","t":"Thanks for the info!\n\nWhy is that? I think in the markepedia article nothing about timeframes is mentioned....","a":"—","d":"","n":"#844","p":34,"im":[],"m":844},{"id":"flaglimits_p34_845","t":"Regarding the question about the FTB and target. You can blindly take the trade when price returns, but I prefer not to. I wait for a engulf so I can be sure that the zone holds.\n\nThe target of your FTB trade depends ill try to draw it:\n\nThe safest target is the one above\n\nThe reason why:\n\nPrice can go all the way to the top box before hitting it's target lower\n\nI hope it is clear, if not, let me know","a":"—","d":"","n":"#845","p":34,"im":["2d9e9b76242d2197f4ca34bb974b7a22ddfcb74a","bb7a02d65f45c62a21a20ea32fa4063227c0f832","b270d7d19030c2efd627462009e1185c1ca1b956","9a0d29013dc15ee2653f8c96876515159a612a21"],"m":845},{"id":"flaglimits_p34_846","t":"thetrendsfriend wrote: Thanks for the info! Why is that? I think in the markepedia article nothing about timeframes is mentioned....\n\nIt is because the FL that is created after the break of an important lvl is the most important, in this case it is the FL that is created after the break of the low. On the 4 hour chart you cant see what happend after the break of the important low, so we must zoom in to get a better look and find our FL.\n\nAlso Ifmyante stated that we must go in the lowest timeframe possible to find the FL, I think he said it on the thread on ForexFactory","a":"—","d":"","n":"#846","p":34,"im":[],"m":846},{"id":"flaglimits_p34_847","t":"When you say you would wait for an engulf, do you mean that prices should engulf the lower edge of the FL after the FTB (for example in your Chart of EURGBP)? To me those FLs look like a swap from resistance to support. If there is a situation like on AUSUSD D1 here:\n\nDoes this mean there's always a FL of indecision on a small timeframe in this case on AUDUSD M1?\n\nSo do we always have to search for FLs on the low timeframes or do we know they are there? Thanks for your help, really want to grasp this:)","a":"—","d":"","n":"#847","p":34,"im":["0151f8b4ef9cbea108142702d8afa978ffa631a5","567616e5426a004171a81b8d1d5de792668eb2a2"],"m":847},{"id":"flaglimits_p34_848","t":"What I meant with waiting for an engulf:\n\nAnd about the AUDUSD:\n\nWe look for the FL in a lower timeframe when we can't see it in the current timeframe","a":"—","d":"","n":"#848","p":34,"im":["924665599461ac07012f47ee1ff66836d3ab3154","10fe4ba10549098cd1a12aca3caa8e7dcd5da8f9","4bb95b52afd4efdd2345cf0e5ac8466a777472e4","853ef8429766914f8fb57b6144b20d97a38e8c6c"],"m":848},{"id":"flaglimits_p34_849","t":"Okay, new try: GBPCAD D1 After the FL is no FTB yet.\n\nGBPCAD M1 Price flags for quite a while until it reaches strong supply and then rallies up\n\ndoes this look fine?\n\nThanks","a":"—","d":"","n":"#849","p":34,"im":["8139740c44b7160dce43c61f3ccd741216d973f6","0afe8bd322d0cfdb7191b1421e74d98793432087"],"m":849},{"id":"flaglimits_p34_850","t":"Hey,\n\nZooming out in the 1 min chart will help a lot!","a":"—","d":"","n":"#850","p":34,"im":["1f7a9a1aef199a977f7e42b15a1e84780b70b782"],"m":850}],"images":[{"k":"885fa214499dd3e132ce9124bbbbb2e9d19f335e","t":"assets/thumbs/885fa214499dd3e132ce9124bbbbb2e9d19f335